{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MISOTextInput","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Layout","anchor":"Layout"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text input is based on several configurable UI elements:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"label","type":"text"}]},{"text":": It is used to describe the purpose of the input.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In some UI contexts, especially when space is limited or when the input is part of a compact layout (search bars, filters, inline forms), the label can be hidden.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, hiding the label should only be done if the purpose of the input remains clear thanks to a placeholder or contextual icon","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and if the label is still accessible to screen readers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Hiding a label is a design choice that must balance visual simplicity and clarity of intent, without compromising inclusiveness or form guidance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"placeholder"}]},{"type":"text","text":": if the text of the text input is empty a placeholder provides a hint or guidance inside the field to suggest expected input."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A prefix and a suffix can be added to give more context."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"leading icon"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": it helps indicate the purpose of the input (magnifying glass for search, envelope for email, phone device for phone number)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only use a leading icon if it adds clear functional or contextual value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"trailing action"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": it is used to provide actions related to the field: clear input, toggle password visibility, open a date picker, etc."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Can also indicate status or feedback (error checkmark, loading spinner)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Outlined style","anchor":"Outlined-style"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", the input is with a subtle background fill and invisible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Best suited for dense layouts or to enhance visibility."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"outlined"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the text input is a minimalist design with a transparent background and a visible stroke outlining the field."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This style may be interesting for contexts other than form pages:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When inputs need to feel lightweight and unobtrusive"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a header (search field)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a selection\/filtering feature in a product catalog","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["   \/\/ An outlined text input","   MISOTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, isOutlined: true)","","   \/\/ With a localizable and a bundle","   MISOTextInput(LocalizedStringKey(\"label_wording\"), bundle: Bundle.module, text: $text)"]},{"anchor":"Rounded-layout","type":"heading","text":"Rounded layout","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Text input can have rounded layouts to be favored in more emotional, immersive contexts or those tied to specific visual identities.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For standard or business-oriented journeys, keep the default corners.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This evolution addresses the need for flexibility in adapting the design to some brand contexts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To activate the rounded corner behavior, set to true the ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasRoundedTextInputs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tuning"},{"type":"text","text":" object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in your theme configuration (if the theme exposes this property at init)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Some themes do not have this flexibility, like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BlueCoatTheme"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Status","type":"heading","anchor":"Status"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Five status are proposed for all layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"default (by default)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Default neutral appearance, whether empty or filled.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It allows users to click, focus, and type freely without restrictions.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"error"}]},{"type":"text","text":": The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" status indicates that the user input does not meet validation rules or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"expected formatting. It provides immediate visual feedback, typically through a red border,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error icon, and a clear, accessible error message positioned below the input. The error messages replaces the helper text."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"loading"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":" state indicates that the system is processing or retrieving data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"related to the text entered. A progress indicator appears to inform the user that an action is in progress."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"readOnly","type":"text"}]},{"text":" :The","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"readOnly"},{"text":", lets the text visible but not editable","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disabled"}]},{"text":": In ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"text":" status, the field is non-interactive and grayed out to indicate it cannot be changed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.disabled()"},{"text":" is ignored.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Helpers","level":2,"text":"Helpers"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper text"}]},{"text":":  A supporting text conveys additional information about the input field,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as how it will be used. It should ideally only take up a single line, though may wrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to multiple lines if required, and be either persistently visible or visible only on focus.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Helper link","type":"text"}]},{"text":": If the helper text is not sufficient, it’s possible to offer the user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an additional help link (the link can be external or open a modal).","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Accessibility considerations","anchor":"Accessibility-considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default no haptics are done by the component for the trailing action."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However you should think about cases wher you will have to make the devices vibrates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can refer to the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/playing-haptics"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Mandatory field indication","anchor":"Mandatory-field-indication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields are mandatory” at the top of your form.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Do not use an asterisk at the end of each field label, nor the word “mandatory.”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If not all fields are mandatory (several fields present): display the message “All fields marked with an * are mandatory” at the top of your form.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use an asterisk (*) at the end of each mandatory field label, and ensures this is well vocalized.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UI rendering of the asterisk must be done with "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"bold font weight","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"negative content color","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (red on light backgrounds)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the mention “(optional)” at the end of each optional field label. Note that this rule is not systematic, it remains an option, to be used if needed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If there is only one field in the form, or if the mandatory nature is obvious (such as login\/password),","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no mention is necessary since the fields are essential to the form’s functionality."}]},{"anchor":"Rich-text","type":"heading","text":"Rich text","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"No other text styles should be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users."}]},{"anchor":"Code-samples","type":"heading","text":"Code samples","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ The text to display and edit","    @State var text: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ Empty text and no placeholder","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text)","","    \/\/ Empty text with placeholder and suffix","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\")","","    \/\/ Empty text with prefix and suffix","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, prefix: \"Distance\", suffix: \"km\")","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon for more context","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\", suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  leadingImage: MISOImage(asset: Image(systemName: \"envelope\")))","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon displayed as raw image (not tinted)","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Brand\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_brand\"), renderingMode: .original))","","    \/\/ Flip the leading icon for RTL layouts using MISOImage.flipped","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_arrow\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))","","    \/\/ Add a trailing button with local image named \"ic_cross\" for additional action","    let trailingAction = MISOTextInput.TrailingAction(image: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_cross\")), actionHint: \"Delete\") { text = \"\" }","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Email\", text: $text, trailingAction: trailingAction)","","    \/\/ With helper text","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Email\",","                  text: $text,","                  placeholder: \"firstName.lastName\",","                  suffix: \"@orange.com\",","                  helperText: \"The email will be automatically completed with @orange.com\")","","    \/\/ With helper link","    @Environment(\\.openURL) private var openUrl","","    let helperLink = MISOTextInput.HelperLink(text: \"Helper Link\") {","       openUrl.callAsFunction(url)","    }","","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text, placeholder: \"Placeholder\", helperLink: helperLink)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need to flip your leading icon for RTL, use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"flipped","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOImage","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["    @Environment(\\.layoutDirection) var layoutDirection","","    MISOTextInput(label: \"Label\", text: $text,","                  leadingImage: MISOImage(asset: Image(\"ic_arrow\"), flipped: layoutDirection == .rightToLeft))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.4.1 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Version"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS 0.20.0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Since"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MISOTextInput"}],"title":"MISOTextInput","externalID":"s:14MISOComponents13MISOTextInputV","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MISOTextInput"}],"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"15.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"13.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0"}]},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOTextInput","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misotextinput"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers